er intoxication), particularly at high cumulative doses. These effects can manifest as congestive heart failure, especially when combined with other cardiotoxic agents like 环磷酰胺 or 放线菌素. The severity and frequency of these side effects underscore the need for careful clinical monitoring during treatment. [Data: Relationships (17124, 17127, 17128, 17131)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Biomarkers such as 肌酸激酶MB and 天冬氨酸转氨酶 reflect 阿霉素-induced tissue damage\",\n            \"explanation\": \"阿霉素 administration affects key clinical indicators of cellular injury. Specifically, it elevates serum levels of 肌酸激酶MB (CK-MB)—a marker of myocardial damage—and 天冬氨酸转氨酶 (AST), which indicates hepatocellular or cardiac injury. However, studies show that co-administration with protective agents like 二氢杨梅素 can significantly reduce the activity of these enzymes, suggesting mitigation of 阿霉素-induced apoptosis and electrophysiological abnormalities in cardiac tissue. This demonstrates the utility of these biomarkers in assessing both toxicity and therapeutic interventions. [Data: Relationships (4821, 4823); Entities (13780, 13467)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Several compounds reverse 阿霉素 resistance by inhibiting P-glycoprotein\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A cluster of agents—including 24-乙酰泽泻醇, ZSTK474, 薯蓣皂苷, and 血根碱—interact with 阿霉素 to overcome multidrug resistance (MDR) in cancer cells. These compounds enhance intracellular accumulation of 阿霉素 by inhibiting P-glycoprotein (P-gp), a key efflux transporter responsible for drug resistance. For example, 24-乙酰泽泻醇 increases 阿霉素 retention in MCF-7/DOX cells in a concentration- and time-dependent manner, while ZSTK474 shows dose-dependent reversal of resistance in HL60/ADR cells. Similarly, 血根碱 downregulates P-gp expression via inhibition of transcription factors, thereby restoring sensitivity to 阿霉素. These findings highlight promising strategies to improve 阿霉素’s therapeutic index. [Data: Relationships (25775, 26584, 50408, 50537)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"放线菌素 exacerbates 阿霉素’s cardiotoxicity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"放线菌素, another antineoplastic antibiotic with inherent cardiotoxic properties, interacts with 阿霉素 in a way that amplifies the risk of congestive heart failure. Clinical evidence indicates that co-administration of cardiotoxic antibiotics like 米托蒽醌, 丝裂霉素, and 放线菌素 with 阿霉素 significantly increases the likelihood of severe cardiac complications, even at lower cumulative doses of 阿霉素. This pharmacodynamic interaction necessitates caution when combining such agents in chemotherapy regimens. [Data: Relationships (53786)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Gut microbiota may influence 阿霉素’s efficacy or metabolism\",\n            \"explanation\": \"阿霉素 exhibits an interaction with 植生拉乌尔菌, a gut microorganism, within the context of microbiome-mediated drug modulation. While the exact mechanism is not fully detailed, the broader evidence cited notes that intestinal bacteria can metabolize or inactivate drugs—such as 球形赖氨酸芽孢杆菌 degrading aspirin or Mak gene–expressing microbes inactivating 阿卡波糖. This suggests a plausible pathway by which 植生拉乌尔菌 might alter 阿霉素’s bioavailability, activity, or toxicity, aligning with emerging research on the gut microbiome’s role in chemotherapy outcomes. [Data: Relationships (53787); Entities (12500)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"阿霉素 belongs to the anthracycline antibiotic class with shared toxicity profiles\",\n            \"explanation\": \"阿霉素 is formally categorized under 蒽环霉素类抗生素, a drug class that includes 表阿霉素 and 柔红霉素. Members of this class share mechanisms of action—primarily DNA intercalation and topoisomerase II inhibition—as well as overlapping adverse effect profiles, notably dose-dependent cardiotoxicity leading to congestive cardiomyopathy. This classification contextualizes 阿霉素’s risks within a broader therapeutic family